cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the thesis below."
title: "Mean-Variance Dynamics and Market Efficiency in Silver: A Multi-Model Forecasting Framework"
abstract: >-
  Companion code for a Master's thesis testing whether weekly silver returns and weekly
  realised volatility are forecastable from past prices and public information, read
  through the efficient-market hypothesis. Covers a classical, tree-based, and
  deep-learning model ladder for the conditional mean and GARCH/HAR/tree models for the
  conditional variance, with sentiment and technical-indicator ablations.
